From 463e6508b614df96d30532d8bef7fdd39446de54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:08:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rv6names: one dnsmasq signalled per names file, a 15 min hold
 and 5 min pacing

IPv6 device names signalled every dnsmasq instance whenever any names file
changed, and dnsmasq's SIGHUP runs cache_reload(), which frees every cached
answer that did not come from a hosts file - on a busy LAN the DNS cache
emptied every few minutes. v6n_reload_br signals only the instance whose
bridge's file changed (no ALL_SDN); rv6n_hold_merge holds a changed set for
15 min before it is written; rv6n_hup_due paces reloads to one per 5 min,
on uptime. Lean: tests/test_rv6names.py (hold and pacing host-executed);
REAPER-FIXES C20.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/rv6names.c           | 131 +++++++++++++++++----
 release/src/router/shared/reaper_v6names.c |  50 ++++++++
 release/src/router/shared/reaper_v6names.h |  33 +++++-
